00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:16.267
-Now, we do this thing every
week where I send out a hashtag

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:18.334
and ask you guys
to respond to that topic.

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:21.467
This week, I sent out
the hashtag "MyWorstCar."

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:22.601
-Oh.

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:24.067
-Asked you guys to
share stories about

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:25.801
the worst car you've ever had.

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:28.501
Within minutes it was a trending
topic, so thank you for playing.

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:30.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:33.834
What was your worst car?
-I had so many worst cars.

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:35.300
-I know.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.901
My grandpa had a car that had a
hole that I could see the --

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:38.234
I could see through.

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:40.267
-See the floor? Yeah.
-I could see the street, yeah.

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:42.567
-My friend had that
and we drove over a puddle

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:45.501
and water shot up
like a fire hose.

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:47.200
One car I had,
the brakes went out.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.267
I was going, "Oh, wow.
The brakes are out.

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:49.334
That's weird."

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:51.300
Downshifted it, parked,
and went...

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.868
[ Gasping ]
-Yeah, exactly.

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:55.701
My dad had a car -- The most
expensive car we ever had.

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:58.667
It was a beautiful car,
velour interior.

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:01.734
-Ooh! Velour.

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:04.434
-Not too hot in the summer,
not too cold in the winter.

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:06.400
Kind of cozy, yeah.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.501
And he was cleaning out
the engine

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.767
or something like that
or something.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.100
-Yeah, with that gunk spray?

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.133
-I think it's called
Gunk Spray, yeah.

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.133
Also, what is he doing?
He shouldn't do that.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:16.200
-You just spray it in
the carburetor,

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.400
try to get it to start.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.033
-Yeah, but he shouldn't do that.
-What happened?

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.267
-He just doesn't know how
to fix cars.

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:21.501
What is he doing?

00:01:21.501 --> 00:01:24.100
So, anyways, he did that,
and it lit fire, right?

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.400
And so he's like --
He freaked out.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.767
He didn't know what to do,
so he closed the hood

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:30.000
thinking that
would put the fire out.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.167
And then it just kept --
It got bigger.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.801
And then he was trying to
open the hood.

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:35.801
It's one of those latches where
you've got to kind of pull

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:38.467
the button and --
And he's burning his fingers

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:39.467
trying to open the hood.

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.000
And then he's like, "I can't."

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.734
And then the neighbor's like,
"You need help, Jim?"

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:44.033
And he's like,
"My car's going to blow up."

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:45.801
And they're like, "What?!
Oh, my God!"

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:48.033
So they ran inside,
and then my dad told us

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:49.033
the car is going to blow up.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:51.701
My mom made us lay on the floor.

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:55.968
She thought the windows
were going to break.

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:57.033
-She's seen the movie, yeah.

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:58.434
-They called
the fire department.

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:01.334
Yeah, he totaled his car.
-Oh!

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:03.033
-That was the last
good car we ever had.

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:04.667
Yeah. Anyways, here you go.

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:07.434
These are going to be worse.
Here we go. My worst car.

